# Mini Information Retrieval Engine

## Focus Area
Information Retrieval Modern AI systems do not generate answers from nothing — they first retrieve relevant information[span_1](start_span)[span_1](end_span). This project builds a mini retrieval engine that accepts user queries and returns the most relevant documents from a knowledge base, ranked by similarity score, with a threshold below which it honestly admits it cannot find anything useful[span_2](start_span)[span_2](end_span).

